<card id="c" title="Zla Kolata and Prokletije: 300 Euros There and Back">
<do type="prev" label="Back"><prev/></do>
<p>First I went looking for a ticket machine. There is one too, it even works and sells tickets with no line, but there&apos;s no platform ticket in the menu, only bus tickets.</p>
<p>So I had to join the line. By the time I got to the front it was already 18:55, and the bus was leaving at 19:10. The platform ticket cost 300 dinars.</p>
<p>I headed to the platform. It was 18:58. I was just walking up to it when the bus started pulling away right in front of me. I waved my arms and ran after it, backpack and all. Caught it and managed to jump on. As it turned out, buses in Serbia don&apos;t stick to the timetable anywhere on the route except the first station, they just move on.</p>
